nodecode-gensyn-ree is a rewrite of TakeshiTGAL's TakeshiTGAL/hermes-gensyn-plugins:

  https://github.com/TakeshiTGAL/hermes-gensyn-plugins
  commit 9325a7b15d815ca05983885ddd6615eae5f2b7a6
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the three tools `ree_validate_receipt`, `ree_verify_receipt` and
`ree_infer`, in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract. The same pinned
image by digest (`gensynai/ree:v0.8.0`), started with `--pull never`; the same
three docker argv (validate with `--network none` and one receipt read-only;
verify with the two weight caches, one receipt and one tasks folder; run-all
for infer, CPU only); the same reading of the official validate's four hash
lines against its exit status; the same comparison of the seven hashes and
the five readable fields, and the same levels and their names.

Left out, and why: the Hermes approval machinery (cron, yolo, single-query,
unattended and host-isolation refusals) is Hermes runtime, so the operator is
asked through Nodecode's own question instead, every time, and only for verify
and infer. The `docker_context` setting, the image-missing message and the
"never pull" rule are kept. The full receipt-schema validator (receipt v2 is
checked on its version, its model name and its hashes, not field by field),
the weight-size estimate from the Hugging Face cache (only the model name is
read), the receipt kept beside a returned one under `~/.cache/hermes-ree`,
and the exact JSON envelopes (`retryable`, `fields`, `next`, `elapsed`) are
replaced by the text block a Nodecode tool answers with. The two skills are
the manual `(help :gensyn-ree)`.
